<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia peso closes up in sluggish session.</title>
<headline>Colombia peso closes up in sluggish session.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's peso gained 0.55 pesos aginst the dollar to close at 1,060.45 in a sluggish session Thursday, interbank traders said.</p>
<p>One trader said the demand from industry was virtually non-existent and said the only real movement was caused by banks shortening dollar positions.</p>
<p>Dealers reported 307 trades worth a total $127.5 million. The peso hit an intraday high of 1,059.6 pesos and sank to a low of 1,061.5.</p>
<p>((--Juan Guillermo Londono, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
